        "silhouettes": [
          { "band": "front", "width_cm": 350, "height_cm": 250 },
          { "band": "left", "width_cm": 700, "height_cm": 250 },
          { "band": "right", "width_cm": 700, "height_cm": 250 },
          { "band": "rear", "width_cm": 350, "height_cm": 250 },
          { "band": "top", "width_cm": 700, "height_cm": 350 }
        ],
        "sensor_height_cm": 150,
        "note": "The line tank with the Mk1 visual sight swapped for the Mk1 thermal one, and nothing else touched: the same five sections, the same armour, the same facet table, the same silhouettes, the same tracked mode and the same two guns, so a match between the two is a match between the sights. The two numbers cut X.3 adds are the thermal term of doc 16 section 9 item 3, keyed on the TARGET's power and speed and multiplied into the ground's own signature factor: a tank under way presents 1000 -- a running engine is the plume this sight is for -- an idling one 650, and a shut-down one 120. At the sight's 45 cells that is 450 m against a moving tank, about 290 m against an idling one and about 54 m against a cold one, which is the whole of \"an idling tank is cold\": shutting down is how a tank hides from it, and standing in woods is not. Version 2 (16b cut M.4): both tracks carry disable_motion_when_all_of, so a tank with no tracks neither drives nor turns."
      }
